  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Since Last Update — 17-Day Catch-Up + Last 48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>US CENTCOM struck IRGC targets at Sirik, Bandar Abbas, Asaluyeh, Jask, and Qeshm Island on September 1; eleven people were killed, including five at a wedding party, per NPR. The IRGC replied on September 2 with ballistic missiles and drones against US positions in Jordan, Bahrain, and Iraq. FM Araghchi's August 19 public statement — "Iran rejects ceasefire and demands a complete end to the war" (Middle East Monitor) — remained the stated public posture entering the UNGA week. Both the ceasefire-commitment forecast (old F2, horizon September 6) and the indirect-session forecast (old F3, horizon September 17) expired without resolution during this period. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Hormuz commercial traffic declined further through September 9–18, with daily transits falling to 7 on September 9 and a 10-day average of approximately 13 vessels per day against the pre-war 85/day baseline (GlobalSecurity Day 203; straits.live Day 203 tracker). Iran's IRGC navy struck the Togo-flagged tanker Trend for unauthorized passage on approximately September 18 (Al Jazeera liveblog); UKMTO separately logged a tanker set on fire by an unknown projectile and a security incident 16 nautical miles off Khasab, Oman on the same day. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>The US approved visas for Iran's core UNGA delegation on September 17, including President Pezeshkian and FM Araghchi, for the high-level debate opening September 22 (Al Jazeera). Senior Iranian official Mohsen Rezaei transmitted Iranian conditions for ending the war to Washington through the Doha channel on September 19 (Al Jazeera liveblog). Iran's government stated on September 20 that participation in UNGA is a "legal right" (IANS) — framing that tracks with sovereignty rather than diplomatic concession language. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>No Iranian ballistic missile or drone attack on a host-country target has been confirmed since the September 8–9 launch of 20 missiles at Jordan's Muwaffaq Salti base, a 9-day pause as of September 18 (GlobalSecurity Day 203 update). IRGC naval operations against commercial shipping at Hormuz continued during the same period, as the Trend tanker strike documents, but those events fall below the classification of a host-country ballistic or drone attack as defined in the resolution criteria. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Five post-registration Israeli polls published by September 17 show Yashar (Eisenkot) averaging 22.2 seats against Likud's 21.2, with Yashar leading in four of the five surveys (Jerusalem Post). Haaretz published a September 17 poll showing Likud's seat count dropping while the pro-Netanyahu bloc narrowly edged ahead at bloc level. An i24NEWS poll on September 9 showed Likud at 27 seats against Yashar's 22, but no subsequent survey replicated that result. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP (computed summary) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
